# Production deploy probes must distinguish initial readiness from loaded assets

The town canvas starts at `ready` with zero tracked assets before its pilot module imports. A byte probe must require a positive loading total before accepting `ready`; otherwise it can freeze an incomplete cue-window response sample. The production measurement and normal/saveData comparison now share this wait in `e2e/asset-diet.spec.ts`.

Observe transient cue visibility inside the page from before entry. Test cold Claim loading in a fresh browser context: navigating there after town permits prefetch/cache to remove the cold cue. Production E1 strips the debug Claim door, so deploy selects only the ordinary player-entry town budget test. Town re-entry and Claim cue behavior remain separately covered in the full build.

Require one desktop and one mobile measurement with matching URL totals; duplicate project output is not two devices. The strict cue-window ceiling stays below 25,000,000 bytes. Settled totals remain evidence only, and physical iPhone/Android SHIP verdicts remain the owner's. The mobile normal/saveData cue-window comparison still failed after the readiness repair (19,537,066 versus 19,300,728); no settled-value substitution or weakened assertion was made.

Evidence and final gate status: `/Users/robin/Claude/Projects/Gold Rush/artifacts/deploy-budget-production-probe/report.md`. At note creation the final dry run and all four full-build cue tests passed; the complete Node battery was still running. No publication or commit was performed.

Related: [[Gold Rush MOC]].

